{
  "answer": "Yes, you can bring your e-cigarette on the plane, provided it complies with the airline's regulations. The e-cigarette must be packed in your cabin baggage, which must meet the size and weight limits specified in our policy. For Classic, Flex, and Business passengers, the cabin bag must not exceed 55 x 35 x 20 cm and 9 kg (Business: 12 kg). Light passengers may add a cabin bag for EUR 20 per flight, up to 6 hours before departure. If you present a cabin bag at the gate without having purchased one, it must be placed in the hold for a fee of EUR 60. If overhead space is full, cabin bags of Classic, Flex, and Business passengers may be placed in the hold at no charge. Please ensure your e-cigarette is properly packed and complies with all safety regulations.",
  "policy_covers_question": true
}
